  "findings": [
    "GameState.SetStartingSide copies the supplied byte without a side validity gate; GameState.GetStartingSide copies the saved byte to output; CardFunctions wrapper forwards it.",
    "OnlineMatch Ubergraph i17047..17213 obtains MatchControllerV2, client-side info and GetActiveSide; passes client info side plus that launch-time active-side result into BP_Logic.StartMultiPlayerGame.",
    "StartMultiPlayerGame copies both event inputs to persistent frame and calls Logic Ubergraph entry40823; span40823..40895 saves LocalPlayerSide and calls GameState.SetStartingSide.",
    "The saved field is read by GetStartingSide rather than recomputing it from EffectContext.Controller, Self, receiver or ongoing GameState.ActiveSide.",
    "Managed query already reads saved StartingSide. However MatchSnapshot omitted it, so ActionJournal.Fingerprint could not distinguish otherwise equal states with different saved starting side.",
    "Current managed constructor/import path still uses Left default while native clear/CDO is0 and launch writes its explicit event value; phase and producer integration remain pending."
  ],
  "repair": {
    "files": [
      "src/KLink.Bot/Engine/GameState.cs"
    ],
    "behavior": "Add StartingSide to MatchSnapshot and Snapshot() initialization, thereby to SnapshotJson and ActionJournal.Fingerprint. No runtime getter/default/import/HTTP/wire behavior changed.",
    "compatibility": "Additive init property; old snapshot JSON missing it deserializes to NotAvailable0. This is not a full engine-state restore API."
  },
